<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Nutrition – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Nutrition</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Healthy Food for a Balanced Diet</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Create a narrative about a memorable event or occurrence. Interactive: Create responses to class survey questions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a short narrative about a memorable meal with family, including traditional Panamanian foods (e.g., "Describe the special Sunday meal of your abuelita's sancocho and rice and explain why it's meaningful to your family.")<br>Can create responses to questions about dietary choices (e.g., "I often eat yogurt because it's healthy and has probiotics that help with digestion.")<br>Can respond to survey questions on food preferences (e.g., "I prefer fruits over other snacks because they are natural and provide more nutrients.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students participate in a quick "Healthy Foods Word Cloud" activity. The teacher displays a blank slide or whiteboard. Students call out or write down any healthy foods they know (e.g., fruits, vegetables, grains, proteins). The teacher writes them to form a word cloud, activating prior vocabulary from previous lessons. Students briefly write one sentence about a food they prefer, for example: "I prefer fruits because they are natural."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing short, clear sentences on the board using the target grammar (modal "should," first conditional, adverbial clauses with "because") and vocabulary. For example: "We <b>should eat</b> more <b>vegetables</b> because they give us <b>vitamins</b>." "If we eat a <b>balanced diet</b>, we <b>stay healthy</b>." The teacher explicitly highlights the grammatical structures and vocabulary for effective writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the modeled structures and vocabulary for writing tasks.<br>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'should' tell us to do?" (Expected answer: It tells us what is a good idea or advice.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When do we use 'because' in a sentence?" (Expected answer: To explain the reason or justification for something.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'balanced diet' mean?" (Expected answer: Eating different types of healthy foods.)</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Nutrition"</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short narrative excerpt (100-120 words) about a memorable healthy Panamanian family meal, or a set of example responses to a dietary habits survey. This text explicitly uses the target vocabulary (e.g., <i>sancocho, nutrients, digestion, metabolism, fiber, protein</i>) and grammar (<i>should, if...then, because</i>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students analyze written texts to identify and understand the use of specific grammar structures and vocabulary related to nutrition and giving advice, preparing them for their own writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (for writing analysis):</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the provided narrative/survey responses individually.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main topic of this text?" "Who is talking about food?" (Students write their answers in their notebooks.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching/Grammar identification:</b> Students underline all sentences that use "should" for advice, circle sentences with the first conditional ("If you eat well..."), and highlight adverbial clauses of justification using "because." They also list 5 new vocabulary words they notice from the text.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>Accuracy focus on Writing</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences focusing on correct use of modal "should" for advice, first conditional for facts, and adverbial clauses for justification. They integrate vocabulary: <i>nutrition, health, benefits, balanced diet, fruits, vegetables, grains, protein, vitamins, minerals, digestion, eat, prefer, improve, consume, advise, healthy, nutritious, beneficial</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion:</b> The teacher provides sentence beginnings or cloze exercises. Students complete the sentences using the target grammar and vocabulary.
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"You __________ (eat / should eat) more _________ (fruits/processed food) because they are rich in __________ (vitamins/calories)."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If you _________ (consume / avoid) sugary drinks, you __________ (will improve / will digest) your __________ (health / metabolism)."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Good _________ (nutrition / fast food) is important __________ (because / if) it helps with __________ (digestion / hunger)."</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled - Guided Sentence Writing:</b> Students write three sentences based on prompts, ensuring they use each target grammar structure at least once.
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Write one piece of advice about a healthy food choice using "should" and "because." (e.g., "You should eat whole grains because they have fiber.")</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Write a fact about healthy eating using the first conditional ("If..."). (e.g., "If you drink enough water, you stay hydrated.")</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Write a sentence explaining the benefit of a specific food using an adverbial clause ("...because..."). (e.g., "Avocados are superfoods because they have healthy fats.")</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Check (Writing-focused):</b> Students exchange their written sentences from activity 2 with a partner. Partners check for correct grammar, appropriate vocabulary use, and clarity. They underline any errors or suggest improvements in writing.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-17 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Nutrition"</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Students will individually produce one of the following written tasks:</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Option A: Short Narrative Composition (Productive Writing):</b> Students write a short narrative (6-8 sentences) about a memorable meal with their family, focusing on traditional Panamanian foods and explaining why it's meaningful to them. They must include at least one sentence using "should" for advice, one using a first conditional, and one adverbial clause with "because." (e.g., "Last Sunday, we had my abuela's delicious sancocho. She always says, 'You should eat this because it has many nutrients.' If you eat a balanced portion, you feel nourished. It's a superfood for our family.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Option B: Survey Response (Interactive Writing):</b> Students respond in writing to 4-5 questions from a "Healthy Eating Habits" survey. They must use target vocabulary and grammar to explain their choices and offer simple advice where appropriate.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is your favorite healthy snack, and why?" (e.g., "I prefer fruits like mango because they are natural and have vitamins.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What types of meals do you usually eat for dinner? Should you improve your choices?" (e.g., "I usually eat rice and beans. Yes, I should add more vegetables because they have fiber.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If you eat a balanced breakfast, what benefits do you experience?" (e.g., "If I eat a balanced breakfast, I stay focused longer during class.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency and effective communication in written form, demonstrating the ability to construct coherent paragraphs or responses using the target grammar and vocabulary accurately to discuss nutrition and healthy eating habits, incorporating Panamanian cultural context.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>Formative assessment strategy</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher uses an observation checklist/simple rubric focusing on the clear and appropriate use of target grammar structures and vocabulary in students' written work. Peer assessment of a specific element (e.g., use of 'should').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their written narrative (Option A) or their completed survey responses (Option B).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Writing):</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Cohesion:</b> Is the narrative/response easy to understand? Are ideas connected logically?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Correct use of "should" for advice, first conditional, and adverbial clauses ("because").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Use:</b> Appropriate integration of target vocabulary (<i>nutrition, benefits, balanced diet, vitamins, protein, digestion, advise, healthy, nutritious</i>).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Task Completion:</b> Does the writing address the prompt and meet the length/sentence requirements?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Spelling and Punctuation:</b> Basic accuracy in mechanics.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket (Writing Reflection):</b> Students complete two sentences on a slip of paper before leaving class:
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I used in my writing today was __________ and it means __________."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I found it (easy/challenging) to write about __________ because __________."</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">7-8 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What aspect of writing about healthy eating do I still need to practice more?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can good nutrition help me in my daily life, based on what I wrote today?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What specific writing elements (grammar, vocabulary, sentence structure) worked well for the students?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What common writing errors or difficulties did students encounter, and what adjustments or scaffolds are needed for subsequent writing tasks or the next lesson? (e.g., more examples for narrative structure, additional practice on adverbial clauses).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How well did the integration of Panamanian cultural context motivate student writing?</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence (Lesson 5 - Mediation & Integration):</b> The written narratives and survey responses from this lesson will serve as foundational material for the next lesson. Students will use their own written output to summarize, compare, or explain information about healthy eating habits and memorable meals to others, potentially leading to a collaborative project or presentation based on their individual writings.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>